1. DEFINITIONS

   "Software" means the Sapphics Structure Library mod, including all source
   code, compiled bytecode, binary assets, file formats, and documentation
   distributed under this license.

   "Proprietary Code" means all source code and compiled classes within the
   package com.sapphic.ssl.internal and any sub-packages thereof, including
   but not limited to: StructureLoaderImpl, BlockUpdateFilter, PaletteCodec,
   TsaphStructReader, TsaphStructWriter, WorldQueueCache, RegionIndex,
   TsaphLootEngine, LootRegistry, and any obfuscated equivalents thereof.

   "Public API" means the interfaces, classes, and types within the package
   com.sapphic.ssl.api and any sub-packages thereof, including but not limited
   to: IStructureLoader, IStructureExporter, ITsaphLootEngine, StructureQueue,
   StructureLoaderBridge, StructurePiece, BlockEntry, PendingPlacement,
   LootTableRef, TsaphLootTable, TsaphLootPool, TsaphLootEntry, LootRange,
   LootEnchantment, RegionMarker, SaphStructFormat, StructureBoundingBox, and
   StructureQueue.

   "Dependent Mod" means any Minecraft mod, plugin, library, or software
   project that calls into the Public API at runtime without reproducing the
   Software's source code or compiled internals.

   "You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
   license.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

2. GRANT OF API USE

   Subject to the terms of this license, Sapphic hereby grants You a
   worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable right to:

   (a) Include the compiled Software (the .jar file) as a dependency of a
       Dependent Mod, whether declared at compile time or runtime;

   (b) Call, invoke, implement, and interact with the Public API in Your own
       source code;

   (c) Distribute Your Dependent Mod to end users, provided the Software is
       either bundled as-is without modification or obtained independently by
       the end user from an authorised source.

   This grant does not convey any ownership interest in the Software.

