   builds. Any attempt to circumvent that obfuscation is itself a violation of
   this license and may constitute criminal unauthorised access to computer
   material under the Computer Misuse Act 1990 (UK) and equivalent legislation
   in other jurisdictions. Violations will be pursued to the fullest extent
   permitted by law.

   (a) Copying, reproducing, publishing, or distributing the Proprietary Code
       in source or compiled form, in whole or in part, in any medium — whether
       the copy was obtained directly, extracted from a distributed .jar, or
       reconstructed by any means including decompilation or bytecode analysis;

   (b) Modifying, adapting, translating, or creating derivative works of the
       Proprietary Code;

   (c) Reverse engineering, decompiling, disassembling, or otherwise attempting
       to derive, reconstruct, or approximate the source code of the Proprietary
       Code, whether by automated tooling, manual inspection of bytecode, or any
       other means. The Proprietary Code is distributed in obfuscated form
       deliberately and with the intent that its internal logic remain
       confidential. Circumventing or defeating that obfuscation by any means is
       a breach of this license and may constitute a violation of applicable law,
       including but not limited to the Computer Misuse Act 1990 (UK) and
       equivalent legislation in other jurisdictions. The sole exception is where
       applicable law expressly and unconditionally permits such activity and
       that right cannot lawfully be waived by contract, and only then to the
       minimum extent required by that law;

   (d) Removing, altering, or obscuring any copyright notice, attribution, or
       proprietary legend included in or with the Software;

   (e) Sublicensing, selling, renting, leasing, or otherwise transferring
       rights in or to the Proprietary Code to any third party;

   (f) Incorporating the Proprietary Code into any product or service that
       replicates or substantially replicates the core functionality of the
       Software as a standalone structure-loading or loot-generation library
       for Minecraft mods;

   (g) Distributing a modified version of the compiled Software .jar under the
       same or a confusingly similar name.

